      "value": "<p>A small locked moon, notable chiefly as the vantage from which the acid haze below was first mapped in depth. Its surface is regolith over basalt with a thin frost of sulphur compounds on the night side. The 2268 mapping party spent four months on it and produced the standard haze atlas.</p>",
